00:41:47.571 --> 00:41:49.273
the next day he'll do
something with Biden.

00:41:49.273 --> 00:41:52.009
And obviously they're
afraid to let him out.

00:41:52.009 --> 00:41:54.111 align:start size:84% position:16%
How is this guy
gonna run the country

00:41:54.111 --> 00:41:57.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
when he does one
appearance, no questions,

00:41:57.314 --> 00:42:00.351
gets back in his car and goes
home for three days and rests?

00:42:00.351 --> 00:42:02.386
He's in a presidential campaign.

00:42:02.386 --> 00:42:05.089 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean how's he gonna
run the country?

00:42:05.089 --> 00:42:07.791
Who's gonna match whits
with Putin or Kim Jong-un

00:42:07.791 --> 00:42:12.129
or what's his name, Xi Jinping?

00:42:12.129 --> 00:42:13.831
He can't do it, he can't do it.

00:42:13.831 --> 00:42:16.033
So what's going on with him?"

00:42:16.033 --> 00:42:18.402 align:start size:97% position:3%
You know, people say that
there are certain medications

00:42:18.402 --> 00:42:20.504
that you know, can
make him more lucid.

00:42:20.504 --> 00:42:24.375 align:start size:88% position:13%
But to me, the
telltale was last night

00:42:24.375 --> 00:42:29.380
when Kamala Harris said,
"The Harris administration

00:42:30.114 --> 00:42:32.249
along with Joe Biden."

00:42:32.249 --> 00:42:33.684
I said to myself,

00:42:33.684 --> 00:42:38.155
"Jeanine, what is going
on in the back rooms?

00:42:39.189 --> 00:42:41.225
What are they planning?

00:42:41.225 --> 00:42:43.827
Why is it that she's
referring to herself

00:42:43.827 --> 00:42:47.364 align:start size:97% position:3%
as the Harris administration
with Joe Biden?

00:42:47.364 --> 00:42:50.768
Is he the entree you
know, just to get in?"

00:42:50.768 --> 00:42:53.337 align:start size:88% position:13%
Because I can't believe
the man is capable

00:42:53.337 --> 00:42:54.972
of running this country.

00:42:54.972 --> 00:42:57.675 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Judge, I don't
know if you saw this.

00:42:57.675 --> 00:43:00.611 align:start position:0%
But like literally about 15
minutes before we started this,

00:43:00.611 --> 00:43:02.246
he flubbed it today too

00:43:02.246 --> 00:43:05.849 align:start size:97% position:3%
and he called it the
Harris-Biden administration.

00:43:05.849 --> 00:43:08.419 align:start size:97% position:3%
Literally, it happened like
15 minutes before we went live

00:43:08.419 --> 00:43:10.387
or before we started recording.

00:43:10.387 --> 00:43:11.221
- Oh my gosh.

00:43:13.991 --> 00:43:15.225
I rest my case.

00:43:15.225 --> 00:43:17.628
Res ispa, the thing
speaks for itself.

00:43:17.628 --> 00:43:20.197
Res ipsa loquitur, little Latin.

00:43:20.197 --> 00:43:21.532
- So let's back up for a second.

00:43:21.532 --> 00:43:24.134
Because you know, Trump
and a lotta my audience,

00:43:24.134 --> 00:43:26.036
you know a bit about
my political evolution

00:43:26.036 --> 00:43:28.472 align:start size:97% position:3%
and that I was a Bernie
supporter and a progressive

00:43:28.472 --> 00:43:30.107
and a lefty and
all those things.

00:43:30.107 --> 00:43:32.409
(chuckles) You're good.

00:43:32.409 --> 00:43:34.211
You're a pro, you're a pro.

00:43:34.211 --> 00:43:37.715 align:start size:97% position:3%
I should be judged accordingly
for all of those things.

00:43:37.715 --> 00:43:39.883
But I know that there's
a lot of my audience

00:43:39.883 --> 00:43:43.454 align:start position:0%
that I would say they don't
consider themselves conservative

00:43:43.454 --> 00:43:44.922
per se or even on the right,

00:43:44.922 --> 00:43:46.957 align:start size:97% position:3%
but they consider
themselves what I would say

00:43:46.957 --> 00:43:49.893 align:start size:84% position:16%
is sort of the
disaffected liberal.

00:43:49.893 --> 00:43:52.796 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I think that is a
huge, huge amount of people

00:43:52.796 --> 00:43:54.064
in America right now.

00:43:54.064 --> 00:43:55.165
The liberals that
just can't believe

00:43:55.165 --> 00:43:57.201
how bananas the left has gone.

00:43:57.201 --> 00:43:59.970 align:start size:84% position:16%
But I think the other
piece of that is

00:43:59.970 --> 00:44:03.641
they just find something
about Trump off-putting

00:44:03.641 --> 00:44:06.510
whether it's the way he speaks
or the tweeting or whatever,

00:44:06.510 --> 00:44:07.578
somethin' like that.

00:44:07.578 --> 00:44:08.812
So since you know him

00:44:08.812 --> 00:44:10.080
and you talked about it
a little bit already,

00:44:10.080 --> 00:44:13.283 align:start size:84% position:16%
if you wanted people
to be more okay

00:44:13.283 --> 00:44:15.986 align:start position:0%
that he does love this country,
that he's a decent guy.

00:44:15.986 --> 00:44:18.422
And it took me a long time
to get there, by the way.

00:44:18.422 --> 00:44:19.857
I think I mentioned
this on your show.

00:44:19.857 --> 00:44:21.592
It wasn't until I
actually met him

00:44:21.592 --> 00:44:23.661 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I had about 10
minutes to talk to him

00:44:23.661 --> 00:44:25.929
that I felt more okay

00:44:25.929 --> 00:44:29.733 align:start size:88% position:13%
when he literally turned
to my husband and I

00:44:29.733 --> 00:44:31.335
and he goes, "You guys are gay?"

00:44:31.335 --> 00:44:32.569
He goes, "That's great.

00:44:32.569 --> 00:44:34.071
Your only problem is
you're too handsome."

00:44:34.071 --> 00:44:36.640
And I thought this is the guy
who says everyone's a homo.

00:44:36.640 --> 00:44:39.076 align:start size:84% position:16%
You know, they say
that he's a homophobe.

00:44:40.244 --> 00:44:41.845 align:start size:84% position:16%
But since you know
him a little bit more,

00:44:41.845 --> 00:44:44.148 align:start size:81% position:19%
yeah, can you just
dive into that?

00:44:44.148 --> 00:44:47.685 align:start size:88% position:13%
- You know, Donald Trump
is not the caricature

00:44:47.685 --> 00:44:48.952
that they make them out to be.

00:44:48.952 --> 00:44:52.022
And you know, there are
certain little vignettes

00:44:52.022 --> 00:44:55.726
that I remember you
know, when my kids.

00:44:55.726 --> 00:44:57.227
We'd go, we'd fly
down to Florida.

00:44:57.227 --> 00:44:58.462
We had a house.

00:44:58.462 --> 00:45:00.230
And of course, he
had Mar-a-Lago.

00:45:00.230 --> 00:45:04.101
And he would say very
quietly to his kids,

00:45:04.101 --> 00:45:05.536
"Don't talk to her like that.

00:45:05.536 --> 00:45:07.171 align:start size:84% position:16%
You don't talk to
your sister like that.

00:45:07.171 --> 00:45:08.272
You don't talk to
him like that."

00:45:08.272 --> 00:45:09.640
Never raised his voice.

00:45:09.640 --> 00:45:11.241
You know, he was always serious.

00:45:11.241 --> 00:45:13.510
And then when he got
a little more upset,

00:45:13.510 --> 00:45:15.612
it would be no emotion.

00:45:15.612 --> 00:45:17.881
"You just lost your allowance.

00:45:17.881 --> 00:45:20.017
Keep it up, keep it up."

00:45:20.017 --> 00:45:22.920 align:start size:88% position:13%
He was always attentive
to their behavior

00:45:22.920 --> 00:45:24.888
and how they acted
toward each other.

00:45:24.888 --> 00:45:29.893
And I'll never forget it was
toward the beginning of school.

00:45:31.295 --> 00:45:33.430
No, the second semester I guess.

00:45:33.430 --> 00:45:35.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he said, "When we
land, we're goin' to Kmart

00:45:35.933 --> 00:45:38.001 align:start size:97% position:3%
to get our school supplies,"
he said to the kids.

00:45:38.001 --> 00:45:40.804
And I'm like, "Donald
Trump goes to Kmart?

00:45:40.804 --> 00:45:41.905
Wow."

00:45:41.905 --> 00:45:43.173
(Dave chuckling)

00:45:43.173 --> 00:45:45.008
When we would walk down
the street in Manhattan,

00:45:45.008 --> 00:45:46.844
we went out with him a lot.

00:45:46.844 --> 00:45:48.345
He was always kind to me.

00:45:48.345 --> 00:45:50.114 align:start size:97% position:3%
He would say to people, "You
know, this Jeanine Pirro.

00:45:50.114 --> 00:45:52.316 align:start size:84% position:16%
She's the DA you know,
from Westchester."

00:45:52.316 --> 00:45:54.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was always on
television for something.

00:45:56.286 --> 00:45:59.289
And he was always more

00:45:59.289 --> 00:46:02.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, he was beholding
and try and get people

00:46:02.459 --> 00:46:05.462
to recognize you instead of him.

00:46:05.462 --> 00:46:07.364
Whenever he saw a cop,

00:46:07.364 --> 00:46:09.700 align:start size:97% position:3%
whenever he saw a construction
worker or a hard hat

00:46:09.700 --> 00:46:11.802
and they were all
enamored with him.

00:46:11.802 --> 00:46:13.303
They were like, "Oh, hi."

00:46:13.303 --> 00:46:16.073
They didn't have phone
cameras maybe back then.

00:46:16.073 --> 00:46:17.975
But they say, "Can
I shake your hand?"

00:46:17.975 --> 00:46:19.777
He would absolutely do it.

00:46:19.777 --> 00:46:21.845
Whenever we'd go
into a restaurant

00:46:21.845 --> 00:46:23.514
and have dinner or something,

00:46:23.514 --> 00:46:25.249
he'd march right
into that kitchen

00:46:25.249 --> 00:46:27.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
and take care of
everybody in the kitchen.

00:46:27.584 --> 00:46:30.621
He is a good, generous man

00:46:30.621 --> 00:46:34.758 align:start size:88% position:13%
and his kids are a
testament to the success

00:46:35.893 --> 00:46:37.294
that he instilled in them.

00:46:37.294 --> 00:46:38.295
Every one of them.

00:46:38.295 --> 00:46:39.630
I mean those kids are smart.

00:46:39.630 --> 00:46:40.864
They're successful.

00:46:40.864 --> 00:46:42.633
They're brilliant,
they really are.

00:46:42.633 --> 00:46:44.601
And as a human being you know,

00:46:44.601 --> 00:46:47.437
you go through tough periods
in your life or your career.

00:46:47.437 --> 00:46:51.108
He was always there for me or
you know, for my then-husband.

00:46:51.108 --> 00:46:53.343
He was always there.

00:46:53.343 --> 00:46:54.778
Always.

00:46:54.778 --> 00:46:56.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
Generous in spirit,
loved his brother Robert.

00:46:56.814 --> 00:47:00.150
I was at the White
House for the wake.

00:47:01.318 --> 00:47:03.554
Was very, very sad about that.

00:47:04.555 --> 00:47:06.857
Very family-oriented day.

00:47:06.857 --> 00:47:08.492
They were always together.

00:47:08.492 --> 00:47:13.497
He was with his sisters and
his brother and never drank.

00:47:15.132 --> 00:47:17.501
And I remember when
I interviewed him
in 2016 right before

00:47:18.569 --> 00:47:20.304
he ran,

00:47:20.304 --> 00:47:22.105
there was talk of him
running and I said,

00:47:22.105 --> 00:47:24.341 align:start size:84% position:16%
"You wanna tell people
you don't drink."

00:47:24.341 --> 00:47:25.275
He said, "No, I don't drink.

00:47:25.275 --> 00:47:26.443
Never had a drink."

00:47:26.443 --> 00:47:27.911
And people were floored by that,

00:47:27.911 --> 00:47:30.914
but I've seen him in all
hours of the day and night.

00:47:30.914 --> 00:47:32.382
Would go Mar-a-Lago.

00:47:32.382 --> 00:47:35.719 align:start size:97% position:3%
Everybody'd be you know,
half in the bag, not Donald.

00:47:35.719 --> 00:47:37.120
Not Donald.

00:47:37.120 --> 00:47:38.622
I love the guy.

00:47:38.622 --> 00:47:41.358
He's a wonderful, wonderful
man and he loves his country.

00:47:41.358 --> 00:47:42.593
And you know what?

00:47:42.593 --> 00:47:44.061
I don't know anyone, Dave,

00:47:44.061 --> 00:47:48.198 align:start position:0%
who could take the assaults
that he's taken on a daily basis

00:47:48.198 --> 00:47:49.166
and survive them.

00:47:49.166 --> 00:47:50.400
The guy looks better than ever.

00:47:50.400 --> 00:47:53.837 align:start size:88% position:13%
Usually after four
years, you're exhausted.

00:47:53.837 --> 00:47:55.472
He's rarin' to go.

00:47:55.472 --> 00:47:56.406
- No, I know.

00:47:56.406 --> 00:47:58.141
He's more bronze than usual now.

00:47:58.141 --> 00:48:00.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
It must be 'cause of
peace in the Middle East.

00:48:00.878 --> 00:48:02.112 align:start size:84% position:16%
It made him bronzer
or something.

00:48:02.112 --> 00:48:04.248
But speakin' of the
human side of things,

00:48:04.248 --> 00:48:06.750
I've had a bunch of
the Fox hosts on.

00:48:06.750 --> 00:48:10.254
And you know, you guys all
just get endlessly trashed

00:48:10.254 --> 00:48:13.557
in the media and you get
the Media Matters boycotts

00:48:13.557 --> 00:48:16.560 align:start size:97% position:3%
and they go for your sponsors
and all of that stuff.

00:48:16.560 --> 00:48:18.528
And I don't know how comfortable

00:48:18.528 --> 00:48:20.030
you'll be talking about this,

00:48:20.030 --> 00:48:23.200
but you did mention to me
once how it can take a toll

00:48:23.200 --> 00:48:25.002 align:start size:84% position:16%
you know, when
you're in your town

00:48:25.002 --> 00:48:26.003
and, "Oh, there's Judge Jeanine.

00:48:26.003 --> 00:48:27.504
She's on Fox,"

00:48:27.504 --> 00:48:29.940
and just dealin' with
some of that kinda hate

00:48:29.940 --> 00:48:31.508
and yet you always have
a smile on your face.

00:48:31.508 --> 00:48:33.677
I mean what's that like?

00:48:34.878 --> 00:48:37.714
You live in New York,
you're a public person

00:48:37.714 --> 00:48:41.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you gotta deal with
some pretty hateful stuff.

00:48:41.618 --> 00:48:42.452
- Yeah, I do.

00:48:42.452 --> 00:48:43.687
I do.

00:48:43.687 --> 00:48:45.055
But you see, the
difference for me

00:48:45.055 --> 00:48:48.325
is I ran for office five times.

00:48:48.325 --> 00:48:52.629 align:start size:88% position:13%
I am hardened with steel
and I'm used to it.

00:48:52.629 --> 00:48:55.198 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean they used to
boycott for this or that

00:48:55.198 --> 00:48:59.102 align:start size:97% position:3%
or I'd prosecuted a case,
they didn't like it, you know?

00:48:59.102 --> 00:48:59.903
You know what?

00:48:59.903 --> 00:49:01.204
I really don't care.

00:49:01.204 --> 00:49:04.841
If you care enough that

00:49:04.841 --> 00:49:07.210
you're thinking about
changing your mind,

00:49:07.210 --> 00:49:09.513
then care and change your mind.

00:49:09.513 --> 00:49:12.549 align:start size:97% position:3%
But if you believe that
what you're doing is right,

00:49:12.549 --> 00:49:14.685
I don't give it
a second thought.

00:49:14.685 --> 00:49:18.655
But what I am amazed at or with

00:49:18.655 --> 00:49:22.392
is the fact that people
on the left dropped me

00:49:22.392 --> 00:49:23.860 align:start size:81% position:19%
you know, when
Trump got elected.

00:49:23.860 --> 00:49:25.162
My friends dropped me.

00:49:25.162 --> 00:49:27.898
And I was like, "But I
would never drop you."

00:49:27.898 --> 00:49:29.766
You know, I just wouldn't.

00:49:29.766 --> 00:49:32.970 align:start size:88% position:13%
It all started you
know, we all got dropped

00:49:32.970 --> 00:49:35.238
and I found that hurt.

00:49:35.238 --> 00:49:37.874 align:start size:84% position:16%
That hurt.
- I know the feelin'.

00:49:37.874 --> 00:49:39.142
- It hurt.

00:49:39.142 --> 00:49:41.078
And you know, when
you try you know,

00:49:42.446 --> 00:49:45.649 align:start size:97% position:3%
to not maybe sound as crazy
and then you just say,

00:49:45.649 --> 00:49:46.483
"You know what?

00:49:46.483 --> 00:49:47.784
I am who I am."

00:49:47.784 --> 00:49:50.020
It's a short visit here, Dave.

00:49:50.020 --> 00:49:52.356
All of us are here
for a short time.

00:49:52.356 --> 00:49:55.525
And if you can't be who you are

00:49:55.525 --> 00:49:57.661
and if you don't
know who you are,

00:49:57.661 --> 00:49:58.929
then you better you know,

00:49:58.929 --> 00:50:02.399
reintroduce yourself to
yourself and get movin'.

00:50:02.399 --> 00:50:04.634
So I have no regrets

00:50:04.634 --> 00:50:07.804 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I also don't worry
about those people

00:50:07.804 --> 00:50:09.172
and I also am a gun owner.

00:50:09.172 --> 00:50:10.307
I have six guns.

00:50:11.475 --> 00:50:14.111
- As you know I am
a new gun owner,

00:50:14.111 --> 00:50:16.880
so we share some
things in common.

00:50:16.880 --> 00:50:21.485 align:start size:97% position:3%
So you end the book fittingly
with a closing statement,

00:50:21.485 --> 00:50:23.920 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
so I feel that we should
end this interview

00:50:23.920 --> 00:50:25.255 line:0%
with a closing statement.

00:50:25.255 --> 00:50:28.325 line:0%
I mean if someone
picks up your book

00:50:28.325 --> 00:50:30.193 line:0%
and we're six weeks now roughly.

00:50:30.193 --> 00:50:31.628
But when the book comes
out about five weeks

00:50:31.628 --> 00:50:33.897
before the election,

00:50:33.897 --> 00:50:36.233
what is it that you
want them to take

00:50:36.233 --> 00:50:38.135
more than anything
else from the book?

00:50:39.603 --> 00:50:42.039
- I want people
to recognize that

00:50:44.307 --> 00:50:45.876
it's not just about the lies.

00:50:45.876 --> 00:50:49.279
I mean I identify the lies
and I go through the lies.

00:50:49.279 --> 00:50:51.648 align:start size:97% position:3%
But the most important
thing for them to understand

00:50:51.648 --> 00:50:54.551
is that there's a quote
from Abraham Lincoln

00:50:54.551 --> 00:50:56.353
from his speech at lyceum

00:50:56.353 --> 00:50:59.156
where he talks about the
destruction of this country

00:50:59.156 --> 00:51:01.425
will not come from
a foreign source.

00:51:01.425 --> 00:51:03.326
It will come from within

00:51:03.326 --> 00:51:05.328 align:start size:84% position:16%
and that's what we're
facing right now.

00:51:05.328 --> 00:51:07.731
We're facing an absolute

00:51:08.899 --> 00:51:11.401 align:start size:84% position:16%
destruction of
America as we know it

00:51:11.401 --> 00:51:15.138
from forces within America
and we can't let that happen.

00:51:15.138 --> 00:51:18.375
We can't forget who we are,

00:51:18.375 --> 00:51:20.310
how free we are

00:51:20.310 --> 00:51:23.747
and we can't not
protect Americans

00:51:23.747 --> 00:51:26.283
and our families
and our businesses.

00:51:26.283 --> 00:51:27.751
You know, we were happy.

00:51:27.751 --> 00:51:28.985
We really were.

00:51:28.985 --> 00:51:30.720
I mean some people
are just miserable.

00:51:30.720 --> 00:51:33.290
But this is really
the land of the free

00:51:33.290 --> 00:51:34.458
and the home of the brave

00:51:34.458 --> 00:51:36.626 align:start size:84% position:16%
and we need to
continue to be that.

00:51:36.626 --> 00:51:38.128
I don't need anyone to tell me

00:51:38.128 --> 00:51:41.331
that America was never so
great or America sucks.

00:51:41.331 --> 00:51:42.732
You know, if you
don't like America,

00:51:42.732 --> 00:51:44.701 align:start size:84% position:16%
well then don't
live here, you know?

00:51:44.701 --> 00:51:47.270
But we can always make changes.

00:51:47.270 --> 00:51:49.506
Evolution is part of who we are,

00:51:49.506 --> 00:51:52.709
but I love this country
and Donald Trump does too

00:51:52.709 --> 00:51:53.510
